# Source archives — we keep the extracted GEDCOMs in git, not the zips
# No, actually, the zips being all like this. The zips should be ignored individually because it makes it so that, as a human, I'm able to see when the zips are there. 

# Generated artifacts. Committed prose lives in reports/, not here.
out/*

# ...except the browsable pages Emma actually works from. This one was lost to a
# fresh clone once: gitignored, with "regenerate rather than commit" written in
# reports/wikidata-unreached.md and no script that could regenerate it. It is
# tracked now, and scripts/build-unreached-page.py rebuilds it from the tracked
# TSV in about a second.
!out/wikidata-unreached.html
!out/wikidata-isolates.html

